            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="0514" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/534: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-01T15:00:00-05:00">December 1, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>394. Your 540, December 1, 1 p.m. You may inform French Foreign Office that I
                    shall be very glad for my part to delay publication until the morning of
                    Tuesday, December 3, and have already made arrangements to that end. You should
                    say however that we have sent communications to Tokyo, London, Berlin and Rome
                    similar to those sent to you and that there is possibility that news will break
                    at any one of those places. Department however is informing those points of
                    delay here.</p>
                <p>I cannot delay the message to the Chinese Government as it has already gone. I of
                    course have no objection to French Government communicating message to Russian
                    Government simultaneously with message of their own. I hope however that message
                    will be transmitted on Monday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
